# Service child-page word highlights

On service detail pages (web, mobile, desktop, cloud, AI, blockchain, and any future `/services/[slug]` child), long body copy must highlight key phrases the same way mobile development does today.

## Markup

- In locale strings, wrap important phrases with double asterisks: `**phrase to highlight**`
- Highlight metrics, outcomes, differentiators, and short lead-in labels (e.g. `**Native iOS and Android development —**`, `**4.5+ star ratings on average**`, `**sub-200ms response times**`)
- Do **not** bold entire paragraphs — only 1–3 short phrases per paragraph (or per why-card description)

## Rendering

- Always render about / why long text through `parseInlineBold()` from `@/lib/parseInlineBold`
- Highlighted text must appear as **bold orange**: `font-bold text-orange-600`
- Do not invent a second highlight style (no underline-only, no purple, no background chips)

## Where it applies

- About sections: `RichAboutBlock`, `WebAboutBlock`, `AboutBlock`
- Why-choose descriptions: `WhyChooseGrid` (already uses `parseInlineBold`)
- Any new long-form text blocks on service child pages must use the same helper

## Locales

- Add `**…**` markers in `en` first, then keep the same markers in other locale files when those strings are English mirrors or when translating (highlight the equivalent important phrase)

## Do not

- Strip `**` markers from mobile (or other) copy when editing
- Leave plain strings in about/why sections without any highlights on a new service child page
- Use Markdown libraries for this — keep `parseInlineBold` as the single path
